EcdsaMethodVerifyContractTest
├── when the guardian answers the magic value
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers the magic value followed by trailing bytes
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers another value
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers true
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers the magic value with dirty low bytes
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers less than one word
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers one byte short of a word
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian answers nothing
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian reverts
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian is asked about the digest
│   └── it should forward the digest and the proof unchanged
├── when the guardian owner signs the digest
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the guardian owner signs a personal message of the digest
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the key of an address with code signs the digest directly
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the key of a delegated address signs the digest directly
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when a delegated address answers the magic value
│   └── it should return the verify selector
└── when code appears or disappears at the guardian address
    └── it should choose the path from the code at verification time
